  "query_preview": "..\n\n- Synoptic Setup:\n\nA low pressure system over Idaho continues tracking east across \nnorthern Wyoming. As this exits east, high pressure moves into the\nregion. A much drier pattern will build through the end work week\nand as southwest flow dominates. As the trough builds off of the \nwest coast, upper riding strengthens over the Northern Rockies \nbringing above normal temperatures through Friday. A shortwave \ntrough pushing across the southeast on Wednesday may bring a \nslight chance for some precipitation. Towards the end of the week\nan upper level trough deepening over the PNW and pushing east \nover the Rockies will push temperatures down closer to normal as \nwell as the next likely chance for precipitation.\n\nThe Flood Watch remains in effect for Dawson, Garfield, Petroleum,\nPrairie, and Wibaux counties through 6PM with additional rain \ntotals between 0.25\" and 0.5\", most of it in the early morning \nhours today. Low clouds presenting as patchy fog may drop \nvisibility to 2 miles in localized areas of higher terrain until\nnoon today, especially along HWY 200, 200S, and 253.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nBlended 6 hours of SREF to better match PoPs with neighbors. No\nchange to NBM otherwise.\n\nLow confidence in additional rain totals exceeding 0.5\" as of 6Z.",
